## 6. Corrected Final Code

```python
def pair_sum(arr, target):
    """
    Brute-force Pair Sum search.

    Returns:
        (i, j) if arr[i] + arr[j] == target
        None if no valid pair exists.

    Time Complexity : O(n^2)
    Space Complexity: O(1)
    """

    n = len(arr)

    # Select the first element of the pair
    for i in range(n):

        # Start from i + 1 to:
        # 1. Avoid comparing an element with itself
        # 2. Avoid redundant mirror comparisons
        for j in range(i + 1, n):

            # Check whether the current pair equals target
            if arr[i] + arr[j] == target:

                # Valid pair found
                return (i, j)

    # Executed only after all possible pairs are checked
    return None
```

